60,3,1,talk,May,,The candidates are here. A is the fare platform. B is the bus corridor. C is station access. D is night service.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,D is impossible. The rosters are empty. We can’t extend hours with this crew.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Midori,,A is a trap. The data says ticketing isn’t the bottleneck. Waiting is.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,C is risky. The pre-war shells hide voids. The contingency pricing will blow the budget.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,A is expensive. The ticketing fees are already too high. The capital ledger is tight.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, D is out. But B? The lane-priority stretches failed before.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, B requires roadway crews. They are a third below establishment. It’s a risk.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, B is a bus route. It doesn’t need the same crews as the rail. It might work.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, B needs roadway consents. The minutes say those are delegated to the authority. That’s good.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, the consents are delegated. But the paving rates climbed. Is B affordable?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, the paving rates are up, but the ferry pilot shows the tech is ready. A is the long-term fix.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, the tech is ready, but the people aren’t. A requires integration. We don’t have the staff.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, A requires data integration. The committee minutes show they can’t agree on data terms.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, exactly. The data deadlock makes A impossible. B is the only option with delegated consents.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, B is the only option that avoids the data deadlock and the pre-war voids.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, I agree. B is the safest bet. It uses the delegated consents and avoids the data issues.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, B is risky for the crews, but it’s the only one that doesn’t require new data agreements.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, B addresses the mid-city crowding. The timed runs show it’s a third longer. It’s a real fix.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, B avoids the pre-war shells. The contingency pricing is safe. I support B.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, B respects the capital ledger. The paving costs are manageable. I vote for B.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
